Found by the k87 worker. In prepareMCPBridges the UNREAL_MCP_URL watcher (waitForEndpoint, 5-minute window) starts right after its own bridge's smoke test, inside the loop. A later stdio bridge's npm install can take up to 5 minutes, so the in-editor server's window can be used up before the editor has even started, and the user gets a false 'not reachable' warning. k87 already starts the http/sse extraServers watchers after the loop for this reason. Done: start the UNREAL_MCP_URL watcher after the loop as well (collect it like the http entries), with a test that a slow later bridge does not eat the window. Lane: unreagent-worker; file cmd/launcher/bridge.go — after k87 lands.

